/* Explanation:

We must visit 7 cities (Riga, Amsterdam, Vilnius, Frankfurt, Bucharest, London, Stockholm) with these required durations:

• Riga: 2 days
• Amsterdam: 2 days (and meet your friend between Day 2 and Day 3)
• Vilnius: 5 days (so that the workshop held in Vilnius on Day 7 falls within your stay – note that Vilnius is scheduled for Days 3–7, with its last day (Day 7) within the [7, 11] workshop window)
• Frankfurt: 3 days
• Bucharest: 4 days
• London: 2 days
• Stockholm: 3 days (with the wedding anywhere between Day 13 and Day 15)

Because the “flight‐day rule” states that when you fly on a day that city A’s visit ends and city B’s visit begins, that day counts for both cities, the overall trip lasts (2+2+5+3+4+2+3) – 6 = 15 days.

The chosen sequence also uses only direct flights. For example:
– Riga → Amsterdam (“Amsterdam and Riga” is available)
– Amsterdam → Vilnius (“Amsterdam and Vilnius” is available)
– Vilnius → Frankfurt (“Vilnius and Frankfurt” is available)
– Frankfurt → Bucharest (“Bucharest and Frankfurt” is available)
– Bucharest → London (“London and Bucharest” is available)
– London → Stockholm (“London and Stockholm” is available)

This plan meets all the duration and event constraints while flying only on routes offered. Enjoy your trip!
